{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788568185916925850,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unamused-cloudy-junebug","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"fbf560c50b4aeabea6d390d4193324a2fcf6b4685d7cfa04f1978811aa0c9b40","event_uuid":"f0b98467-6473-471f-b533-c9057372617e","position":{"commit_sha":"3f705ee0678132ed053391514efb49462b9b0e4f","position":"1788550863426099001-f0b98467-6473-471f-b533-c9057372617e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d4d5ac933d5aa271b794778fd3e50472d548c4f15d79c52d25eef8f713c0cabb","event_uuid":"71acb4e7-eda5-4deb-9b4c-773e28eebb8e","position":{"commit_sha":"0d64c814b588c07eefe543c7c243294c24b0463b","position":"1788560512315722001-71acb4e7-eda5-4deb-9b4c-773e28eebb8e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788550863426099001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"71acb4e7-eda5-4deb-9b4c-773e28eebb8e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ea66-45ea-6f7c-4c73"}],"description":"## The defect\n\n`infra/terraform/user_data.sh` asserts the mount for the GATE-SCRATCH volume but not for the\nGERRIT DATA volume:\n\n- gate-scratch: `mountpoint -q` at `:115`, which FATALs with \"refusing to leave gate scratch on\n  the ROOT filesystem\".\n- `/var/gerrit` (`:88-92`): **no assertion at all.**\n\nBoth fstab entries use `nofail`. And `mount -a` returning 0 does NOT mean the mount happened —\n`nofail` skips quietly. That was PROVEN by execution in a sandbox: stubbing `mount` to return 0\nwithout mounting is exactly the documented nofail-skip mode, and the gate-scratch path caught it\nwhile nothing would catch it for `/var/gerrit`.\n\nSo a `/var/gerrit` mount that silently does not take leaves **Gerrit running on the root\nfilesystem**, with nothing raising and nothing asserting.\n\n## Why this is the more serious instance of the class\n\nThis is the same silent-fallback-to-root failure that ADR 0112 exists to prevent — but on the\nMORE valuable volume. Consequences of Gerrit running on root:\n\n- The Gerrit repository data goes to a 60 GiB root volume rather than its dedicated 50 GiB one.\n- Root disk pressure returns. Root has already hit **97%** once (2026-09-02), which took Gerrit\n  fully offline for five hours.\n- Backups silently cover the wrong thing: the DLM policy snapshots the DATA volume. If Gerrit is\n  actually writing to root, the daily snapshots contain nothing of value, and root is not on a\n  schedule at all.\n\nThe asymmetry between the two mounts looks unintentional rather than considered — the gate-scratch\nassertion was added by ADR 0112's work, and the older `/var/gerrit` path simply never got one.\n\n## IMMEDIATE RELEVANCE: a Gerrit stop/start is pending\n\nAn approved `terraform apply` will update `aws_instance.gerrit`'s `user_data` and, per provider\nv5.100.0 defaults, STOP/START the instance. On restart, `mount -a` runs against the real fstab. If\n`/var/gerrit` silently fails to mount, **Gerrit comes back up on the root filesystem and nothing\nsays so.**\n\nMitigation until this is fixed: after any instance stop/start, explicitly verify\n`mountpoint -q /var/gerrit` (and `findmnt -no SOURCE /var/gerrit`) BEFORE declaring the host\nhealthy. Do not rely on Gerrit responding as evidence that its data volume is mounted — it will\nrespond either way.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 - `user_data.sh` asserts `mountpoint -q /var/gerrit` after `mount -a`, and FAILS LOUDLY\n      when the mount did not take, in the same shape as the gate-scratch assertion at :115.\n- [ ] AC2 - Defect-seeded: with `mount` stubbed to return 0 WITHOUT mounting (the real nofail-skip\n      mode), the sequence aborts. Removing the assertion must make that test RED.\n- [ ] AC3 - The failure is distinguishable from a genuine mount error: a reader can tell \"the\n      volume did not mount\" from \"mount reported an error\", since nofail makes the former silent.\n- [ ] AC4 - A running-host check exists that an operator can invoke after a stop/start to confirm\n      both volumes are mounted where expected, without reading the script. Portable: no dependence\n      on a specific CI provider or on AWS APIs.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNot removing `nofail` from either fstab entry — `nofail` is deliberate, so a missing volume does\nnot wedge boot. The fix is to ASSERT after mounting, not to make boot fragile.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","ea66-45ea-6f7c-4c73"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9c93-754e-b641-48d1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"user_data.sh asserts the gate-scratch mount but NOT /var/gerrit, so a silently-skipped nofail mount leaves Gerrit running on the root filesystem undetected","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f0b98467-6473-471f-b533-c9057372617e","71acb4e7-eda5-4deb-9b4c-773e28eebb8e"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788568185916925850,"uuid":"e5b4a9ab-a411-442e-ad3a-c5618236a134"}